title: "pallet-conviction-voting: stop counting nay capital as support in `Tally::from_vote`"

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      `Tally::from_vote` set `support: capital` for every vote, so a standard nay vote produced
      a tally whose support included the nay capital. `support` is documented as the number of
      aye votes pre-conviction, and `Tally::add`, `remove`, `increase` and `reduce` all leave it
      untouched for nay votes, so support seeded this way could never be removed again. It is now
      zero unless the vote is aye, matching `Tally::add` on an empty tally.

      `from_vote` has no callers in this repository, so no on-chain tally changes.

crates:
  - name: pallet-conviction-voting
    bump: patch
